# We will calculate multiple population genetic metrics for the different species, such as nucleotide diversity (Pi),
# heterozygosity, Dxy, Fst (absolute and relative divergence) using pixy and plink2 and two different VCF files.
# For pi, dxy, fst, we can use pixy, but for het, we use plink2.
# One VCF file is the one filtered on individual depth and the other one an upstream file including multiallelic SNPs.
# We will also do 2 approaches, namely a whole-genome analysis as well as a window-based approach using 50 kb windows.
# For this, we need to extract sample names from the VCF file to be used to calculate the different metrics.
# Note, sample sizes will differ between the files because some samples have been excluded in downstream filtering steps.
# Also note, the VCF file is not LD pruned!



